      <Patch Id="F3dTs4DAFvpuIGqW1gN1oJ">
        <Canvas Id="U0ZyxRkpRiwfKAw8KAp9ak" CanvasType="Group">

          <Pad Id="CKZndGiH5v9LUQSP6f4RG4" Bounds="60,40,560,60" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="One map tile, fetched and drawn.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;The tile appears on its own: the Cache region has to evaluate once to produce an output at all, so the fetch happens on the first frame. Force re-fetches. Either way it is requested once rather than once per frame, which the OSM tile usage policy forbids.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;GIS.Skia works in pixels from the top-left of the view. VL.Skia does not: its default space is about 2.8 by 2 units with the origin at the centre, so a pixel position of 278 lands nowhere near the window. ToRendererSpace converts between the two -- compare the two rows of readouts below.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;The Renderer's Space pin is left alone deliberately. An unrecognised value there is silently replaced by the default, so converting the numbers is the arrangement that cannot fail quietly. ClientBounds reports in the current space's units, which is how you check.">
            <p:TypeAnnotation>
              <Choice Kind="TypeFlag" Name="String" />
            </p:TypeAnnotation>
            <p:ValueBoxSettings>
              <p:fontsize p:Type="Int32">11</p:fontsize>
              <p:stringtype p:Assembly="VL.Core" p:Type="VL.Core.StringType">Comment</p:stringtype>
            </p:ValueBoxSettings>
          </Pad>

          <Pad Id="OXb8aKeI14IWP608yGjWCA" Comment="Longitude" Bounds="60,140,62,15" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="139.7">
            <p:TypeAnnotation LastCategoryFullName="Primitive" LastDependency="VL.CoreLib.vl">
              <Choice Kind="TypeFlag" Name="Float64" />
            </p:TypeAnnotation>
          </Pad>
          <Pad Id="OuAWHniWdPwNkR3l9LdCrG" Comment="Latitude" Bounds="140,140,62,15" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="35.68">
